<body>

  <!-- Title Header -->
  <div class="header-title">
    <h1>NutriSure</h1>
    <p>3-Module Supplement Certification Platform (Firebase Powered)</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt; color: #94a3b8;">BCA 2nd Year Project • User, Company & Admin Modules with Real-Time Cloud Sync</p>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Project Summary:</strong> NutriSure is an independent supplement certification and marketplace platform. Powered by Google Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore, it provides real-time cross-device data synchronization across three modules: User Marketplace (<code>index.html</code>), Company Proposal Portal (<code>company.html</code>), and Admin Management Panel (<code>admin.html</code>).
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 1 -->
  <h1>1. The 3 Types of Users in NutriSure</h1>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">User Type</th>
      <th style="width: 20%;">HTML Module</th>
      <th>Features & Responsibilities</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Normal User (Customer)</strong></td>
      <td><code>index.html</code></td>
      <td>Browses certified supplements, filters by Budget vs. Premium, filters by Category (Protein, Creatine, Preworkout, Fish Oil, Vitamins), views verified lab test certificates, adds items to cart, and signs in with Firebase Auth.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. For Company (Brands)</strong></td>
      <td><code>company.html</code></td>
      <td>Brands fill out the product proposal form (Name, Product Name, Email, Category, Price, Image, Product Description). Below the form, companies can view their submitted products with real-time cloud status tracking: <strong>Pending 🟡</strong>, <strong>Accepted 🟢</strong>, or <strong>Rejected 🔴</strong>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Admin (Superuser)</strong></td>
      <td><code>admin.html</code></td>
      <td>Protected by password (<code>admin123</code>). Admin reviews pending company proposals with <strong>"✅ Accept & Add to Store"</strong> (which publishes the product to the live customer store via Firestore) and <strong>"❌ Reject"</strong>. Admin can also add products directly with <strong>Product Images</strong> and delete live products.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <!-- SECTION 2 -->
  <h1>2. Complete Workflow: Company Proposal to Admin Approval</h1>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Step 1: Company Submits Product</strong><br>
    A supplement manufacturer visits <code>company.html</code> and submits their product details. The application is pushed directly to Firebase Cloud Firestore (<code>company_requests</code> collection) with status: <code>PENDING</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 2: Admin Receives Proposal in Real Time</strong><br>
    Admin logs into <code>admin.html</code> (Password: <code>admin123</code>). Firestore's real-time listener automatically renders the proposal on Admin's screen without page refresh.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 3: Admin Review (Accept or Reject)</strong><br>
    <ul>
      <li>If Admin clicks <strong>"✅ Accept & Add to Store"</strong>: Admin enters the verified lab score. The product is added to the <code>products</code> collection in Firestore, and status is updated to <code>ACCEPTED</code>.</li>
      <li>If Admin clicks <strong>"❌ Reject"</strong>: The proposal status in Firestore is updated to <code>REJECTED</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Step 4: Real-Time Sync to All Friends & Devices</strong><br>
    All customers globally immediately see the approved product on <code>index.html</code> on their mobiles and laptops!</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- SECTION 3 -->
  <h1>3. Google Firebase Integration Architecture</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Firebase Authentication:</strong> Secure user sign-in and account registration (Email/Password & Google Sign-In) with automatic session persistence.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud Firestore:</strong> Real-time NoSQL database storing <code>products</code>, <code>company_requests</code>, and <code>user_logins</code> collections.</li>
    <li><strong>Real-time <code>onSnapshot</code> Listeners:</strong> Pushes new products, deletions, and status updates instantly to all connected web clients without page reloads.</li>
    <li><strong>Offline Resiliency:</strong> If internet connectivity is interrupted, NutriSure seamlessly falls back to <code>localStorage</code> cache.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- SECTION 4 -->
  <h1>4. Top Viva / Exam Questions & Model Answers</h1>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Q1: What are the different user roles in your web project?</strong><br>
    <em>Answer:</em> Our project has 3 user roles:
    1. <strong>Normal User:</strong> Browses and purchases certified supplements on <code>index.html</code>.
    2. <strong>Company User:</strong> Submits supplement proposals for blind testing on <code>company.html</code> and tracks application status.
    3. <strong>Admin:</strong> Authenticates via password on <code>admin.html</code> to accept/reject company proposals, manage products with images, and view user logs.
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Q2: How does Google Firebase integrate into this project?</strong><br>
    <em>Answer:</em> We integrated Firebase Authentication for user accounts and Cloud Firestore for real-time synchronization. When an Admin adds or accepts a product, Firestore pushes the update live to all connected devices without page reloading.
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Q3: How is product image support implemented?</strong><br>
    <em>Answer:</em> We support direct file uploads from computer/phone using the HTML5 <code>FileReader</code> API (converting photos to Base64 Data URLs), external image URLs, and built-in vector presets, with safe fallback handling on image load errors.
  </div>

  <hr style="margin-top: 30pt;">
  <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #64748b;">
    <strong>NutriSure Firebase Architecture Documentation</strong> • Created for BCA 2nd Year Examination & Viva Demonstration
  </p>

</body>
</html>
